{"title":"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the small country of Mathland, all automobile license plates have four symbols. The first must be a vowel (A, E, I, O, or U), the second and third must be two different letters among the 21 non-vowels, and the fourth must be a digit (0 through 9). If the symbols are chosen at random subject to these conditions, what is the probability that the plate will read \"AMC8\"?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/b/48be44381859d7b892d929f255d28e8741e6d24a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{1}{22,050} \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } \\frac{1}{21,000}\\qquad \\textbf{(C) } \\frac{1}{10,500}\\qquad \\textbf{(D) } \\frac{1}{2,100} \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } \\frac{1}{1,050}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"575\" height=\"40\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>There is one favorable case, which is the license plate says \"AMC8.\"  We must now find how many total cases there are.  There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> choices for the first letter (since it must be a vowel), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> choices for the second letter (since it must be of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> consonants), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> choices for the third letter (since it must differ from the second letter), and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> choices for the digit.  This leads to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/c/4dce44621d0279daf7de6497450cd52d56960674.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\cdot 21 \\cdot 20 \\cdot 10=21,000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"183\" height=\"17\" /> total possible license plates.  Therefore, the probability of a license plate saying \"AMC8\" is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a9c3e3a5b952ceaa1a6c95c84145094834649e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } \\frac{1}{21,000}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"104\" height=\"51\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The probability of choosing A as the first letter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7caa92dbceea7263c9f7cf923ae73853ac9220.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />.  The probability of choosing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> next is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/6/9d614bc78837d1f4f18a57495bd15cfb1f853a78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />.  The probability of choosing C as the third letter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/a/4aa28f834c030baccbf92522582c7a4dde606cdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> (since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> other consonants to choose from other than M). The probability of having <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as the last number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/3/eb3e0d1f799a4917a9ba4ea5dd4a5408cf58ba3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />.  We multiply all these to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0967856f630bf0fa9b30f184f4b5bbedbf628b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{5}\\cdot \\dfrac{1}{21} \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{20}\\cdot \\dfrac{1}{10}=\\dfrac{1}{5\\times 21\\times 20\\times 10}=\\dfrac{1}{21\\times 100\\times 10}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}~\\dfrac{1}{21,000}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"541\" height=\"51\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/fW34t6eFKAU\">https://youtu.be/fW34t6eFKAU</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/JR0B2727ro8\">https://youtu.be/JR0B2727ro8</a> (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8\" title=\"2015 AMC 8\">2015 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2015\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 